{"name":"Iron Ore","hex":"#af5b46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iron ore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral deposit from which iron can be viably extracted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron_ore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iron ore","blocks":[{"text":"Iron ores are rocks and minerals from which metallic iron can be economically extracted. The ores are usually rich in iron oxides and vary in color from dark grey, bright yellow, or deep purple to rusty red. The iron is usually found in the form of magnetite (Fe3O4, 72.4% Fe), hematite (Fe2O3, 69.9% Fe), goethite (FeO(OH), 62.9% Fe), limonite (FeO(OH)·n(H2O), 55% Fe), or siderite (FeCO3, 48.2% Fe)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/HematitaEZ.jpg/330px-HematitaEZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_ore","wikidata":"Q191552"},{"title":"Iron","blocks":[{"text":"Iron is a chemical element; it has symbol Fe and atomic number 26. It is a metal that belongs to the first transition series and group 8 of the periodic table. It is, by mass, the most common element on Earth, forming much of Earth's outer and inner core. It is the fourth most abundant element in the Earth's crust. In its metallic state it was mainly deposited by meteorites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron","wikidata":"Q677"},{"title":"Ore","blocks":[{"text":"Ore is natural rock or sediment that contains one or more valuable minerals, typically including metals, concentrated above background levels, and that is economically viable to mine and process. Ore grade refers to the concentration of the desired material it contains. The value of the metals or minerals a rock contains must be weighed against the cost of extraction to determine whether it is of sufficiently high grade to be worth mining and is therefore considered an ore. A complex ore is one containing more than one valuable mineral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Banded_iron_formation.png/330px-Banded_iron_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ore","wikidata":"Q102798"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/LightningVolt_Iron_Ore_Pellets.jpg/500px-LightningVolt_Iron_Ore_Pellets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/LightningVolt_Iron_Ore_Pellets.jpg/500px-LightningVolt_Iron_Ore_Pellets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stockpiles of iron ore pellets like this one are used in steel production.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightningVolt_Iron_Ore_Pellets.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Iron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_%28page_1%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration of iron ore being unloaded at docks in Toledo, Ohio","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIron_Ore_Docks%2C_Toledo%2C_Ohio_-_DPLA_-_165fedc210b0851a390b4d490563cb43_(page_1)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg/500px-Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg/1280px-Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg/500px-Black-band_ironstone_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Banded iron rock, estimated at being 2.1 billion years old","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack-band_ironstone_(aka).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/TaconitePellet.JPG/500px-TaconitePellet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/TaconitePellet.JPG/1280px-TaconitePellet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/TaconitePellet.JPG/500px-TaconitePellet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Processed taconite pellets with reddish surface oxidation used in steelmaking with a US quarter (24 mm [0.94 in] diameter) shown for scale","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaconitePellet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Iron_ore_prices